	abstract = {The IoT and Artificial Intelligence (AI) will revolutionize solar energy management by producing smarter, more efficient, and sustainable energy systems. The world demand for clean and sustainable energy has precipitated the rapid use of solar energy. However, it is still a big challenge to make it as efficient and reliable as possible. In this chapter, the author describes how the Internet of Things (IoT) and Artificial Intelligence (AI) played a revolutionary role in the sunlight energy system to transcend these limitations. The chapter is a useful contribution to the field of understanding that more intelligent solar energy management relies on technological advances, architectures, and intelligent approaches. Beginning with the disadvantages of the conventional solar systems, the chapter explains how the combination of IoT and AI can enable a reinvention of the solar packing procedure, in which real-time monitoring, predictive analysis, and dynamic energy management are involved. The state-of-the-art literature review follows the evolution of research on IoT-enabled systems of renewable sources and AI-oriented optimization methods and illuminates the gaps in the research. Such innovations are described in the main sections, which outline the design of an IoT-based solar monitoring (sensor implementations, edge computing, and cloud-based data) and analyzers. It also examines the application of AI technologies, such as machine earning, to predictive maintenance, deep learning to panel diagnostics, generative AI to irradiance prediction, and reinforcement learning to optimize the system. Integrated IoT-AI architectures have use cases that are described in terms of diverse applications, including residential applications, as well as utility-scale applications. It contains the practical case studies highlighting the successful deployments, followed by a detailed delving into the technical issues, security concerns, and the latest trends, including the in