	abstract = {Rising concerns about fossil fuel reliance and its environmental impact have driven a global shift toward sustainable energy solutions, with electric vehicles (EVs) positioned as a key solution to both the energy crisis and environmental challenges. At the heart of this transition lies the need for precise battery modeling and state estimation, which are critical for maximizing energy efficiency, extending battery lifespan, minimizing operational costs, and ensuring the safe and reliable performance of EVs. However, precise state of charge (SOC) estimation remains a significant challenge due to the dynamic and nonlinear behavior of batteries. Traditional approaches often fall short in handling the complex variability in SOC models. This study proposes a hybrid deep learning model that combines recurrent radial basis function (RRBF) networks with particle swarm optimization (PSO) to enhance SOC estimation accuracy. The results demonstrate that the proposed model reduces prediction error by 0.48% outperforming conventional methods, including RRBF networks paired with K-means clustering. By addressing critical limitations in SOC estimation, this research contributes to advancing battery management technologies, marking a pivotal step toward more sustainable and efficient energy systems in the electric vehicle sector.  © 2025 IEEE.},
