	abstract = {Alongside the rapid growth of wind power installation, wind curtailment is becoming more serious in China. As a type of clean and high-energy-density secondary energy, hydrogen will play a vital role in large-scale energy storage in future low-carbon energy systems. Incorporating hydrogen energy storage into integrated energy systems is a promising way to enhance the utilization of wind power. Therefore, a bi-level optimal configuration model is proposed in which the upper-level problem aims to minimize the total configuration cost to determine the capacity of hydrogen energy storage devices, and the lower-level problem aims to minimize the operational cost considering the change in hydrogen production efficiency. Owing to the non-convex characteristic of the lower-level problem containing integer variables, the bi-level model cannot be directly converted into a single-level model. Hence, a data-driven surrogate algorithm is applied to solve this complex bi-level programming problem. Case studies show that the proposed method can increase the economic and environmental benefits and improve energy efficiency. Sensitivity analysis is performed to investigate the influence of investment cost and carbon emission price on the results. The correctness and effectiveness of the proposed algorithm are verified by comparison with the particle swarm optimization algorithm. © 2024 Elsevier Ltd},
