re are 544 °C, 4.35 bar, 158.12 bar, and 52.82 bar, respectively. At these conditions, the total hybrid system's energy efficiency, exergy efficiency, exergy destruction, net generated power, and total investment cost rate are 45.96%, 46.83%, 215.72 MW, 203.67 MW, and 9791 $/h, respectively. The findings of this paper conclude that it is necessary to address all objective functions simultaneously in the system's ultimate optimum design. Furthermore, the objective of this paper becomes even more apparent when there is no choice but to cut greenhouse gas emissions while also addressing the rising global energy demand. © 2022},
